source: cli/tests/help.rs
expression: text
---
Clear the tree log (usable if it's corrupted and prevents mount)

The log tree is used for fsync durability. If it becomes corrupted it can
prevent the filesystem from mounting. Clearing it discards the log, so changes
that were fsynced after the last transaction commit are lost. Everything up to
that commit is kept.

The device must not be mounted.

Usage: zero-log <DEVICE>

Arguments:
  <DEVICE>
          Path to the btrfs device

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
